# Line endings are NOT normalised in this repository, deliberately.
#
# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true by default, which would rewrite every text file to
# CRLF on checkout. This repository exists so that anyone can diff it against the upstream
# projects it vendors, and multimon/PROVENANCE.md promises that multimon/ is byte-identical to
# upstream multimon-ng apart from eight documented patches. A CRLF checkout would turn that
# diff into thousands of whitespace hits and hide the real ones.
#
# `-text` means: store the bytes as they are, hand them back as they are. multimon/ keeps the
# LF endings upstream ships; rtl-sdr/ and libusb-andro/ keep the CRLF they were vendored with.
* -text
